.TH CRUNCH_CLOCK_NANOSLEEP 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
crunch_clock_nanosleep \- Linux x86-64 syscall 230
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int crunch_clock_nanosleep(int clock, int flags, const struct timespec* requested, struct timespec* remaining);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes the raw clock_nanosleep syscall; unlike libc clock_nanosleep, errors return -1 and set errno.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clock_nanosleep (2)
